11:["$","p",null,{"children":["Rather than a passive text, the Gita is an intense dialogue taking place on a battlefield—a profound metaphor for the ethical and moral struggles of human life. At the brink of the Kurukshetra war, Prince Arjuna is overcome with despair regarding the violence and death his war against his own kindred will cause. He turns to his charioteer and guide, Lord Krishna, for answers. Check out our"," ",["$","$L1f",null,{"href":"/what-is-dharma","eventLabel":"gita_guide:intro:dharma","trackPathName":"dharma","className":"text-primary font-medium hover:underline","children":"guide on Dharma"}]," ","for more context."]}]
